TBD - 0.3
- Bugfix: Complete the Qt6 migration. The N1MM parser compared the QXmlStreamReader
  name(), a QStringView in Qt6, against string literals, so the program did not build.
- Bugfix: QSO never initialised its Utilities pointer, so every call made through it
  was undefined behaviour. QSO now owns and releases that object, as KLog does.
- Bugfix: The band of a QSO coming from WSJT-X was looked up from the frequency
  truncated to a whole number of MHz, against a table with only nine HF bands. QSOs on
  60m, 6m, 4m, 2m, 70cm and above were stored with no BAND at all. The lookup now uses
  the frequency ranges of KLog's band table.
- Bugfix: A QSO logged from WSJT-X across 00:00 UTC was dated on the day it ended,
  because the date was taken from the QSO end time. The start time is used now.
- Bugfix: QSO::setBandRX() wrote to (and QSO::getBandRX() read) the TX band, so setting
  the RX band silently overwrote BAND. The QSO now keeps a separate RX band.
- Bugfix: Locator::getLocator() negated the longitude, returning mirrored locators.
- Enhancement: Callsign validation now uses KLog's Callsign class, replacing the
  hand-written prefix table. Validation was also unreachable: it was gated on an
  uninitialised global that was always false, so every callsign was accepted.
- Enhancement: Locators are accepted in any case and the latitude/longitude returned
  is the centre of the square, so a locator survives a coordinate round trip.
- Enhancement: The QSO end date/time, BAND_RX, SUBMODE and FREQ_RX are only exported
  when they differ from their QSO start / TX counterparts, as KLog does.
- Enhancement: TIME_OFF, OPERATOR and TX_PWR sent by WSJT-X are no longer discarded.
- Maintenance: A BAND or BAND_RX of "0" is dropped in one single place, so no export
  path can emit an invalid band (same rule as KLog's Adif::getADIFField()).
- Maintenance: Fix leaks of the Utilities and QSO objects held by ADIFForField,
  UDPServer, ParseWSJTX and ParseN1MM.
- Maintenance: Build as C++17, which is what Qt6 requires.

Mar 2026 - 0.2
- Migrated to Qt6

Nov 2022 - 0.1
- First "release" of the software.
- Receives QSOs from N1MM and stores the data in an ADIF file.
- Receives QSOs from WSJTX and stores the data in an ADIF file.
